      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "HTML::FormHandler versions before 0.410002 for Perl render field attributes into HTML without escaping using the process_attrs method.\n\nAny application with fields or field labels where some attributes are built from data rather than literals allows attacker-influenced text in an attribute value that can override the field attributes or embed JavaScript in rendered pages.\n\nFor example, the RadioGroup widget uses the process_attrs method via the render_option and wrap_radio methods.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
